## Original Content
Berlin entend doter son armée d’un arsenal de frappe à longue portée pour faire face à la menace russe aux frontières de l’Otan, selon des documents secret défense consultés par le média américain Politico.

## Summary
Germany plans to invest 12 billion euros in a defense initiative to develop long-range strike capabilities, including cruise missiles and hypersonic gliders with ranges exceeding 2000 kilometers, aimed at deterring Russia along NATO borders. The information is based on secret defense documents reported by Politico.

## Key Points
- Germany is investing 12 billion euros in long-range strike weapons.
- The arsenal includes cruise missiles and hypersonic gliders with over 2000 km range.
- The goal is to counter the Russian threat at NATO borders.
- Details come from secret defense documents cited by Politico.


